A '''glow squid''' is a variant of the normal [[squid]] found in dark underwater areas, typically in [[ocean]] depths, [[canyon]]s, and [[Aquifer|underground lakes]]. It has an aqua luminescent texture, and is the only source of [[glow ink sac]]s.

== Spawning ==
{{IN|Java}}, schools of 4 to 6 glow squid spawn in [[water]] (source block or flowing) in complete darkness in the [[Overworld]] below [[Altitude|layer]] 30, except for [[deep dark]] and [[Sulfur Caves|sulfur cave]] biomes. Unlike most other aquatic mobs, they do not require water or waterlogged blocks above or below their spawning space. In all spawnable biomes, the spawn weight is {{frac|10|10}} and the spawn chance is 100%.

{{IN|Bedrock}}, glow squid spawn anywhere in any [[dimension]] where there's water underground,<ref name="glow_squid_bedrock">{{bug|MCPE-130734}}</ref> in schools of 2 to 4 (below a solid roof categorized as cave spawn, while squid are surface spawns) anywhere below Y=30 in a light level of 0 except [[deep dark]] biomes. The spawn weight is 10 in all spawnable biomes except [[mangrove swamp]], in which the spawn weight is 100.

Glow squid have a 5% chance of spawning as babies.

